      "title": "Software engineer who takes web platforms from architecture to production operation, with React on the front end and Node.js, Python and Java APIs behind it.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "document": "2026-08-30_cv_EN",
          "said": "Software engineer who takes web platforms from architecture to production operation, with React on the front end and Node.js, Python and Java APIs behind it. Two platforms designed, built and operated at HEIG-VD reached daily institutional service. One has carried high-stakes exam sessions since 2022 across 20+ courses and 1,000+ students a year, and every professor who took it up stayed. The CIIP intercantonal education platform's Kubernetes workloads on Exoscale were mine to deploy, configure and release. Earlier, application ownership with change and release governance across a globally used business-application portfolio at Nestle Globe IS/IT. AI-assisted development has been daily practice since GitHub Copilot's 2021 technical preview. Agents write, per-technology review skills read the code back, and the test suites gate what merges. Feasibility studies for armasuisse and Planair concluded that the self-hosted open models of the time fell short, and recommended against them."
        },
        {
          "document": "2026-09-09_cv-en_ownership-application-management",
          "said": "Software engineer who owns business applications end to end, functionally and technically, and keeps them running in production, on Java Spring Boot, Node.js and Python back ends with React and Vue front ends. At Nestle Globe IS/IT, technical owner and SPOC of ~120 globally used business applications, 6 of them business-critical: L3 sustain, accredited Change Board approver and go-live lead inside a formal change and release process. At HEIG-VD, designed, built and owned the school's exam and lab platforms through four years of production, and on the CIIP platform worked as the developer engineer of an agile team, from feature redesigns and API rework to releases on Kubernetes, urgent fixes travelling a dedicated hotfix lane. AI-assisted development has been daily practice since 2021, everything the agents produce reviewed and tested before it ships."
        }
      ]
    },
